Z||000000||Philphine||06-17-2001||12:59 PM||||<BR>i've been looking at the old threads for pulling the engine from the top but i have two questions.<P>one reason i want to pull it (beside the fact that it's a dead 4cyl and i don't want to fix it or have it fixed) from the top is to leave the tranny and suspension in place and hopefully be able to roll the car around if i need to. is that possible? <P>also, at this point i don't know whats going in (it's my long term chop top project). say in a best (or worse depending on how you look at it) case scenario i got a small block for it. would it go back in from the top or would i then have to go ahead and and do the reinstall from the bottom? a caddy engine (pre n* or n*) or one of the various v6's? <P>thanks for any help or opinions.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (project. or at least an interesting collection of parts)||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-17-2001||01:27 PM||||I ripped my 4 out and put my v6 in from the top.. it can be done.. takes 2 people minimum to get it in/out..   one to hoist, one to move it while its lifting..<P>You can change it without taking the tranny out. just takes time and patience to get everything lined up on the tranny. <P>Anything bigger then a 2.8L I would recommend you dropping it from below because you dont have much room to fit it through the top.<P><BR>Good luck!!   <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||06-17-2001||03:21 PM||||Philphine, try this link: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/topswap.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/topswap.html</A> <BR>Doug Kinney of the Fiero Warehouse does it this way, swears it's easier.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||06-17-2001||05:15 PM||||The 4 and 6 have both been done from the top... A V8, forget it... V8's are all shoe horn jobs.<P>As for moving around... you don't need the tranny or axles in to do that. Just the wheels and cradle. The wheels are held solely by the hub units. the axles go inside the hubs.<P>Unless you are ready to shove in another motor, I'd leave it alone for now. To many things get damaged lost or forgotten if you leave it appart for long. It's just the way things are in a project like that.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||06-17-2001||06:39 PM||||I've always dropped the whole thing out the bottom, I've done it at least ten times. Last week I decided to try something different and take a 4 cyl out the top. I read all the info I could find here and it sounded easy enough so I did it. I will <B>never</B> do it again. IMO it is far easier to just drop the whole cradle. If I want to roll the car around, I have spare cradles and struts to bolt in.<BR> <BR>I agre with ogre about leaving the car together until you're ready to do something with it. The more you take apart, the more space it takes up.<P>BTW, the cadillac 4.9 is about 2 inches longer than a 4 cyl and a helluva lot wider. It will never fit in through the top.||||reg||13
Z||000005||Philphine||06-17-2001||06:42 PM||||ok. thanks for the info. i kinda just wanted to try it 'cause i got a come along type thing and i wanted to try it out. plus fooling with this engine i don't care about i thought i would get a feel for doing something kind of major. maybe i'll hold off.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||V8Dreamer||06-18-2001||09:23 AM||||I'm with Rockcrawl on this one, I was helping him put the engine back in through the top, and have helped him with many of his other conversions that came out the bottom.......I would never recommend taking anything out the top, the bottom is soooo much easier.  Plus, don't you want to install some urethane while that cradle is out???<P>Ryan||||reg||1
